# nr-tui-term-frame: wire lines for mixdog-term (native/core/crates/mixdog-term): cell grid, frame writer, painter, selection, VT test grid

Nothing is registered and no protocol method is added: this is library code of the terminal UI.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Package `mixdog-term`: its `dependencies` list gains two entries, after `"mixdog-js",` and before `"portable-pty",`:

    "mixdog-termtext",
    "mixdog-tui-style",

`vte` is already in the list. It moved from `[dev-dependencies]` to `[dependencies]` of the manifest, because `src/testing.rs`
(the VT test grid, `pub mod testing` in lib.rs) is part of the library that the tests of the crates above it use. Both new
dependencies are workspace members that are already `[workspace.dependencies]` entries (`mixdog-termtext`, `mixdog-tui-style`),
so `native/core/Cargo.toml` needs no line. There is no new dependency cycle (neither crate depends on mixdog-term).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Nothing (mixdog-term does not carry the workspace-hack line).

## compose_flip.rs / protocol tables

Nothing.

## What this task could not compile in the workspace

cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). The new modules were compiled and tested outside the workspace with rustc and
clippy-driver in D:\mixdog-build\mig\scratch-nr-tui-term-frame (real vte 0.14.1, real serde_json 1.0.154, the real width and
colour-level sources of mixdog-termtext and mixdog-tui-style, a stand-in for mixdog-js, and stand-ins for the four stub files of
mixdog-termtext that `nr-tui-termtext-ansi-wrap` fills in): 43 unit tests, the 9 tests of frame_stability.rs and the 3 tests of
selection_twin.rs pass, and `clippy -W clippy::all -D warnings` is clean over the library, its unit tests and both integration tests.

The painter's unit tests (src/paint.rs) call `mixdog_termtext::ansi::tokenize` and `mixdog_termtext::wrap::wrap_text`, which are
`unimplemented!` stubs until `nr-tui-termtext-ansi-wrap` lands: they pass against the stand-ins used outside the workspace and
need that task's real implementations in the tree to pass there. Nothing else of this task calls them.

## For the tasks that use this crate

* `mixdog_term::frame::{Grid, Cell, Style, Color, Rect, FrameWriter, PacedFrames, FramePacer, TUI_FRAME_MS, CursorPos}`;
  `FrameWriter::new(out, color_level)` takes the level `ColorEnvironment::level()` decided once at start; `set_synchronized(false)`
  for an output that is not a terminal; `resize()` on a terminal size change; `force_full_repaint()` for the clear-and-repaint on a
  mouse press (dismisses Windows Terminal's native highlight) and on session replacement; `finish()` shows the cursor at exit.
* `mixdog_term::paint::{Painter, RoundBorder, TextWrap}`: text (with SGR and OSC 8 in it), fills, round borders, the right-aligned
  hint overprint. `PacedFrames::new(writer, on_flush)` reports every flushed frame (the render acknowledgement of
  `render-timing.mjs`); the run loop owns the timer and calls `poll(now_ms)`.
* `mixdog_term::selection::{SelectionState, SelectionRect, apply_selection, word_rect_at, line_rect_at, PaintQueue,
  clip_selection_rect}`. The interval of the motion throttle is a constructor argument (`PaintQueue::new(ms)`, default
  `SELECTION_PAINT_INTERVAL_MS` = 24): the caller that reads `MIXDOG_TUI_SELECTION_PAINT_MS` (the mouse task) passes it in; the
  selection band (`selectionClipBand`, which needs the transcript window's row ranges) is ported with the transcript window task.
